The Basics

The Corporate AI Engineer is a hands ‑ on technical role responsible for building, integrating, and operationalizing AI ‑ enabled solutions across the enterprise. This role focuses on delivery and execution, turning&nbsp;prioritized&nbsp;AI use cases into secure, scalable, production ‑ ready capabilities that drive measurable business value. &nbsp;

As a core&nbsp;AI-solution&nbsp;delivery member of&nbsp;Enterprise Architecture team,&nbsp;the Corporate AI Engineer partners closely with&nbsp;IT,&nbsp;Security, Data, and Business teams to move AI&nbsp;solutions&nbsp;from&nbsp;idea to&nbsp;pilot to&nbsp;measurable&nbsp;enterprise impact. &nbsp;

Join us if you are passionate about&nbsp;leveraging&nbsp;AI to drive meaningful outcomes and if you thrive in a growing,&nbsp;collaborative&nbsp;and innovative environment. &nbsp;

This position follows the Company’s hybrid schedule which currently requires employees to work in the office at one of the following locations a minimum of three days per week: Addison, TX; Bellevue, WA; Durham, NC; Emeryville, CA; or Reston, VA.

What you'll do

• Design, build, and deploy AI-enabled solutions aligned to&nbsp;prioritized&nbsp;use cases.

• Implement AI workflows, integrations, and automations across enterprise platforms (e.g., Microsoft 365, Salesforce, ServiceNow)using best-in-breed AI technology from Anthropic, OpenAI, etc. &nbsp;

• &nbsp;Translate architectural designs and business requirements into working AI solutions, including prompt engineering, orchestration logic, retrieveal augmented generation (RAG) patterns. &nbsp;

• Integrate AI solutions with enterprise data sources and systems of record, ensuring data quality, accuracy, and&nbsp;appropriate access

• Own operational readiness of AI solutions, including monitoring, logging, performance tuning, and ongoing optimization.

• Partner with Security, Privacy, and IT teams to ensure AI solutions comply with enterprise governance, risk, and compliance requirements. &nbsp;

• Develop and maintain technical documentation, runbooks, and reusable implementation patterns. &nbsp;

We’re looking for someone with

• 4+ years of experience in software engineering, platform engineering, data engineering,&nbsp;application management,&nbsp;or a similar hands-on technical role.

• Demonstrated experience building, integrating, or operating production systems in an enterprise environment. &nbsp;

• Hands-on experience implementing AI-enabled solutions, including generative AI concepts such as prompt engineering, embeddings, or RAGwith best-in-class AI technologies from OpenAI, Anthropic, ServiceNow, Microsoft,&nbsp;etc &nbsp;

• Experience working with APIs, integrations,&nbsp;MCPs,&nbsp;and enterprise SaaS platforms.

• Working knowledge of AI-related risks, including data security, privacy, model limitations, and cost considerations.

